Bugfix: A reset mail that fails before sending no longer blocks the next request

The password reset stored its token before the mail was put together. When
building the mail failed, for example while rendering its templates, the token
stayed stored and every new request within the next five minutes counted as a
repeated one: no mail was sent, but the page reported success. The token is
now stored right before the mail is handed to the mail server, so such a
failure leaves the account as it was before the request.
